---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { networkCommsSchema, networkCommsTitle, networkCommsDescription } from '../../../lib/expertise-schemas';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={networkCommsTitle}
  description={networkCommsDescription}
  schema={networkCommsSchema}
  ogImage="/images/og/network-communications-expert-witness.jpg"
>

  <div class="hero-banner">
    <h1>Dr. Tal Lavian, Ph.D.: Network Communications Protocols, Architectures and Systems</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-full">

        <p class="facet-line">Part of Dr. Lavian's <a href="/communications-expert-witness/">communications technology practice</a>. <span class="facet-links"><a href="/Dr-Tal-Lavian-CV-Expert-Witness-Network-Communications-Telecommunications-Internet-Protocols-Mobile-Wireless-2026.pdf">Curriculum Vitae (PDF)</a> · <a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">Case history</a> · <a href="tel:+14082099112">+1 (408) 209-9112</a></span></p>

        <p>Dr. Tal Lavian, Ph.D. is a network communications expert specializing in network communications protocols, architectures, and systems.</p>

        <div class="two-col-text-img">
          <div>
            <p>He holds a Ph.D. in Computer Science from UC Berkeley, specializing in network communications, and spent nearly 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing there, including research in data center networking (RAD Labs), network service architectures (SAHARA), and wireless systems (ICEBERG). At Nortel Networks (1996&ndash;2007) he was Principal Scientist and Principal Architect, designing network communication systems. He is the inventor of more than 120 <a href="/patents/">patents</a> and has filed declarations in more than 90 PTAB proceedings (IPR and CBM). He has testified in court cases before judges and juries in U.S. federal and state courts. His publications are indexed on <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=DDVtnHEAAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <img src="/images/heroes/network-communications-expert.webp" alt="" width="360" height="184" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"/>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Technology Areas</h2>

        <div class="expertise-grid">
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/network-communications-expert-witness/">Network Communications</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Network communications and Internet protocols; packet switching, data networks, network architectures.</li>
              <li>IETF, IEEE, ITU-T, and ISO standards.</li>
              <li>Datalink, network, and transport layers (L2, L3, L4); OSI layers 1-7.</li>
              <li>LAN and WAN technologies: IEEE 802.1, 802.3, 802.11, 802.15.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/internet-expert-witness/">Internet Protocols (TCP/IP)</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>TCP/IP suite, TCP, UDP, IP, MAC, Ethernet.</li>
              <li>LDAP, ARP, DNS, DHCP, RIP, OSPF, GRE, VPN; IPv4 and IPv6.</li>
              <li>Core and edge routers, switches, load balancers.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/routing-switching-expert-witness/">Routing and Switching</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Routing and switching systems, architectures, tunneling, and VPN.</li>
              <li>RIP, BGP, MPLS, OSPF, IGMP, IGRP, and IS-IS.</li>
              <li>Router, switch, gateway, content switch, L4-L7 switch, and load balancer architecture and design.</li>
              <li>QoS, priority queuing, traffic classification, and congestion control.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/voice-over-ip-voip-expert/">VoIP and Streaming Media</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>VoIP protocols and systems, IP telephony: SIP, RTP, RTCP.</li>
              <li>Video/audio conferencing and streaming.</li>
              <li>Jitter, packet loss, and network delay.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/pstn-voip-expert-witness/">PSTN</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>PSTN, POTS, PBX, circuit switching, SS7.</li>
              <li>SONET and SDH, WDM, DWDM, and optical transport.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/computer-networking-expert-witness/">Computer Networking</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Web applications, HTTP, e-mail (SMTP, POP, IMAP), and file transfer (FTP).</li>
              <li>Client-server and distributed computing; web services and Internet architecture.</li>
              <li>Firewalls, ACLs, and virtual private networks.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/network-management-expert-witness/">Network Management</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Network Management Systems (NMS), device management, and configuration.</li>
              <li>MIBs, traps, logs, SNMPv2, SNMPv3, and monitoring.</li>
              <li>Alarms, alerts, topology maps, and reporting.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/mobile-wireless-expert-witness/">Mobile and Wireless</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Wi-Fi 802.11, WLAN, mobile devices, and smartphones.</li>
              <li>SMS, MMS, and instant messaging (chat).</li>
              <li>MAC, PHY, ARQ, HARQ, QoS, and queuing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-card">
            <h3><a href="/communications-expert-witness/network-security-expert-witness/">Network Security</a></h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Firewalls, VPNs, IPsec, tunneling, content filtering, security gateways, IDS, and IPS.</li>
              <li>SSL/TLS, SSH, HTTPS, PKI, and digital certificates.</li>
              <li>Authentication, authorization, encryption, and network access control.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Selected Matters</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/case/20-spherix-v-cisco-systems/">Spherix v. Cisco Systems</a>: U.S. Patent Nos. RE40,467, 6,697,325, 6,578,086 and 6,222,848; network protocol and packet switching technologies.</li>
          <li><a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">Corrigent Corp. v. Arista Networks</a>: U.S. Patent Nos. 7,593,400 and 7,545,740; network switching and transport.</li>
          <li><a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">WSOU Investment v. Huawei Technologies</a>: U.S. Patent Nos. 6,882,627 and 7,508,755; network communication systems.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Retained in over 90 cases by over 50 <a href="/law-firm-clients/">law firms</a> and <a href="/corporate-clients/">corporate clients</a>.</p>

