        <!-- FAQ Section -->
        <section class="faq-section" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about Dr. Lavian's network communications work">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <details open>
            <summary>What network communications topics has Dr. Lavian addressed?</summary>
            <p>TCP/IP protocol stacks, Ethernet, LAN/WAN architecture, routing protocols (BGP, OSPF), network switching, and quality of service (QoS) in patent litigation.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What are Dr. Lavian&rsquo;s qualifications in network communications?</summary>
            <p>A Ph.D. in Computer Science from UC Berkeley specializing in network communications; nearly 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing at UC Berkeley; Principal Scientist and Principal Architect at Nortel Networks (1996&ndash;2007); and 120+ invented patents.</p>
          </details>
        </section>

